Reproduced on Flutter 3.47.4 stable (9584c6713b), Chrome on macOS. The `updateChildren` move loop is unchanged on master 697012a97f (links below).

When the web engine reorders a semantics node's children, `SemanticsObject.updateChildren` moves the non-stationary children with `insertBefore` / `append`. If one of the moved subtrees contains `document.activeElement`, Chrome blurs it to `<body>` with no related target. The engine then reports the view as unfocused and the framework parks focus on the root scope, so keyboard shortcuts such as Escape stop working.

One way to hit it is a `Tooltip` overlay opening while a `MenuAnchor` menu is open: the overlay's children are reordered and the open menu's subtree is moved.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Build the code sample below for web (`flutter build web --profile`), serve it, open it in Chrome and turn semantics on. Either use a screen reader or run `document.querySelector('flt-semantics-placeholder').click()` in the console.
2. Activate the "Superset" button through its semantics node, the way a screen reader or Playwright does: a DOM click on its `flt-semantics` element. The pointer ends up over the button. The menu opens and the autofocused "Superset" item takes focus.
3. Wait about 0.5 s, until the hover tooltip "Change the kind" opens.
4. Press Escape.

### Expected results

Focus stays on the autofocused "Superset" menu item, and Escape closes the menu.

### Actual results

Focus is on the menu item at first. About 310 ms later, when the hover Tooltip opens, focus drops to `<body>` and the `focusout` has `relatedTarget = null`. Escape then does nothing.

A pointer press does not hit this, because the press suppresses the hover tooltip. Under a screen reader's activation, the engine's `ClickDebouncer` turns the click into `SemanticsAction.tap`, so the Tooltip never sees a press.

Without the `Tooltip`, focus stays in the menu.

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(
  MaterialApp(
    theme: ThemeData(tooltipTheme: const TooltipThemeData(waitDuration: Duration(milliseconds: 350))),
    home: const Scaffold(body: Center(child: KindMenu())),
  ),
);

class KindMenu extends StatefulWidget {
  const KindMenu({super.key});
  @override
  State<KindMenu> createState() => _KindMenuState();
}

class _KindMenuState extends State<KindMenu> {
  var kind = 'Superset';

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => MenuAnchor(
    menuChildren: [
      for (final k in ['Group', 'Superset', 'EMOM'])
        MenuItemButton(autofocus: k == kind, onPressed: () => setState(() => kind = k), child: Text(k)),
    ],
    builder: (context, controller, _) => Tooltip(
      message: 'Change the kind', // remove the Tooltip and focus stays in the menu
      child: TextButton(
        onPressed: () => controller.isOpen ? controller.close() : controller.open(),
        child: Text(kind),
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

</details>

### Screenshots or Video

Not applicable: the logs below are the evidence.

### Logs

<details open><summary>Logs</summary>

Each focus line reads `<performance.now() in ms> focusin|focusout <event target> rel=<relatedTarget>`. `flt-semantic-node-5` is the "Superset" button and `flt-semantic-node-11` is the autofocused "Superset" menu item.

```
150ms after open: active flt-semantics#flt-semantic-node-11[button]
1s after open:    active BODY
menu still open after Esc: true
3980 focusin  flt-semantics#flt-semantic-node-11[button] rel=flt-semantics#flt-semantic-node-5[button]
4296 focusout flt-semantics#flt-semantic-node-11[button] rel=null
```

Two more things were observed in a real app with a `MutationObserver`:

- The overlay's children went from `[page, menu]` to `[menu, page, tooltip]`. The longest increasing subsequence kept `page` stationary and moved the `menu` subtree with `insertBefore`.
- The unminified stack at the `focusout` was `SemanticsObject.updateChildren <- EngineSemanticsOwner.updateSemantics <- … PipelineOwner.flushSemantics`.

</details>

<details><summary>Playwright script that produced the log</summary>

Serve the web build of the code sample and point `page.goto` at it.

```js
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

const d = `(e) => !e ? 'null' : e === document.body ? 'BODY' : e.tagName.toLowerCase() + (e.id ? '#' + e.id : '') + (e.getAttribute && e.getAttribute('role') ? '[' + e.getAttribute('role') + ']' : '')`;

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch({ channel: 'chrome' });
  const page = await (await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 900, height: 700 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 })).newPage();
  // Log every focusin/focusout with its target and relatedTarget.
  await page.addInitScript(`window.__log = []; const d = ${d}; window.__d = d;
    for (const t of ['focusin', 'focusout']) document.addEventListener(t, (ev) => window.__log.push(Math.round(performance.now()) + ' ' + t + ' ' + d(ev.target) + ' rel=' + d(ev.relatedTarget)), true);`);
  await page.goto('http://localhost:8080/', { waitUntil: 'load' }); // wherever build/web is served
  await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
  // Turn semantics on.
  await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('flt-semantics-placeholder')?.click());
  await page.waitForTimeout(800);

  const active = () => page.evaluate(() => window.__d(document.activeElement));

  // A screen reader's activation: a DOM click on the button's semantics node (Playwright moves the mouse there too).
  await page.locator('flt-semantics[role=button]').first().click();
  await page.waitForTimeout(150);
  console.log('150ms after open: active', await active());
  await page.waitForTimeout(900);
  console.log('1s after open:    active', await active());
  await page.keyboard.press('Escape');
  await page.waitForTimeout(500);
  console.log('menu still open after Esc:', await page.evaluate(() => [...document.querySelectorAll('flt-semantics')].some((e) => e.textContent.trim() === 'EMOM')));
  console.log((await page.evaluate(() => window.__log.splice(0))).join('\n'));
  await browser.close();
})();
```

</details>

### Cause

- In the engine, [`SemanticsObject.updateChildren`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/9584c6713b324636289d067944a46fd6b49df14b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L2165-L2196) computes a longest increasing subsequence of the children that stay, and moves every non-stationary child with `element.insertBefore(child.element, refNode)` or `element.append(child.element)`. Moving a subtree that contains `document.activeElement` makes Chrome blur it with no related target. The [same loop on master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/697012a97f5d094a68015b177cf86216dd007073/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L2241-L2255) is unchanged and has no focus handling.
- [`ViewFocusBinding._handleFocusout`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/9584c6713b324636289d067944a46fd6b49df14b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/platform_dispatcher/view_focus_binding.dart#L60-L74) sees `activeElement == body` and passes the null `relatedTarget` on, so [`_handleFocusChange`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/9584c6713b324636289d067944a46fd6b49df14b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/platform_dispatcher/view_focus_binding.dart#L89-L113) reports the view as unfocused. On master, [`_handleFocusout`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/697012a97f5d094a68015b177cf86216dd007073/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/platform_dispatcher/view_focus_binding.dart#L85-L122) defers a blur with no related target, but only on iOS Safari and only for the active text-editing element (#189744). A semantics button in Chrome is still reported at once.
- In the framework, [`didChangeViewFocus`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/9584c6713b324636289d067944a46fd6b49df14b/packages/flutter/lib/src/widgets/view.dart#L261-L265) then parks focus on `FocusManager.instance.rootScope`, so keyboard shortcuts such as `DismissIntent` have no target.

### Suggested fix

Do what #192963 did for `_updateRole` ([master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/697012a97f5d094a68015b177cf86216dd007073/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L2421-L2480)). Before the move loop in `updateChildren`, record `domDocument.activeElement` when it is inside `element`. After the loop, if `activeElement` changed and the recorded element is still connected inside `element`, call `focusWithoutScroll()` on it.

A cheaper alternative is to choose the moved set so that the subtree containing the active element stays stationary. That works when that subtree is in the intersection of the old and new children, but not in general.

### Workaround

An app can undo the blur from a capturing `focusout` listener on `document`: when `relatedTarget` is null, `document.hasFocus()` is true, and the target is a `flt-semantics` element that is still connected, call `target.focus({preventScroll: true})` inside the handler. Because something other than `<body>` then holds focus, `ViewFocusBinding._handleFocusout` ignores the event and the framework never parks focus. The listener must skip a blur during a Tab keydown, or Tab and Shift+Tab off either end of the page are pulled back and the keyboard can never leave.

### Related issues

- #192792 is the role-change twin of this bug: focus is lost when a role change reparents the focused element's ancestor in `_updateRole`. It is fixed on master by #192963, which preserves focus in `_updateRole` only, not in `updateChildren`. That fix is not in 3.47.4.
- #122876 (open) is a broader report of the same symptom: "accessibility focus is lost after navigating to detail screen".
- I searched for `web semantics reorder children focus`, `web semantics insertBefore focus`, `web overlay tooltip focus lost semantics`, `web menu focus lost screen reader` and `web semantics updateChildren`. None of the results matched the reorder path.

